{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.WedderburnMassFormula","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.WedderburnMassFormula","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Units.Defs"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.extremal_irreps_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.extremal_irreps_count","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-mass-formula.lean#L86-L107","doc":"The number of extremal irreps of S_n is exactly 3 for n ≥ 3:\ntrivial [n], sign [1^n], and standard [n-1,1].\nFor n = 2: trivial and sign only (standard = trivial).\nThe transfer matrix is 2×2 (standard rep), giving 2 invariants\n(trace and determinant). The sym/alt ratio gives the third.\n\nFor n ≥ 4, additional irreps exist (one per partition of n),\nbut the three extremal invariants capture the dominant physics.\nThe interior partitions (hooks) contribute subdominant corrections\nidentifiable with meson exchange channels. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.beta2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.beta2","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-mass-formula.lean#L81-L84","doc":"`β₂ = -2 [3]_q` is derived from the baryon quantum number. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.quantumInt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.quantumInt","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-mass-formula.lean#L62-L79","doc":"The quantum n-integer `[n]_q = (q^n - q^{-n})/(q - q^{-1})`,\nin any commutative ring carrying a unit `q` and its inverse.\n\nOn `R = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` this is the genuine Laurent-polynomial\n`q`-integer.\n\nBase ring (AGENTS.md §7c): stated over a bare `CommRing`.  Both\nthe substrate parameter and the denominator are carried as\n**units** — `q : Rˣ` (so `q⁻¹` is the units inverse, never a\nfield inverse) and `d : Rˣ` pinned by `hd : ↑d = q - q⁻¹` — so\nthe quotient is the division-free product `(qⁿ - q⁻ⁿ) · d⁻¹`.\nThis replaces the old `[Field R]` + `hq : q * q ≠ 1` form, which\nadditionally admitted the junk case `q = 0` (there `hq` holds\nwhile `q⁻¹ = 0`, so the \"quotient\" silently collapsed to `0/0`).\nOver a field the two agree: take `d = Units.mk0 (q - q⁻¹) _`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.atomicMass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.atomicMass","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-mass-formula.lean#L54-L60","doc":"The atomic mass from the Wedderburn formula, valued in the\nground ring `R`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:wedderburn-mass-formula","label":"thm:wedderburn-mass-formula","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-mass-formula.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.MassParams.β₃","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.MassParams.β₃","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-mass-formula.lean#L52-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.MassParams.β₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.MassParams.β₂","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-mass-formula.lean#L51-L51","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.MassParams.α","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.MassParams.α","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-mass-formula.lean#L50-L50","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.MassParams.m_n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.MassParams.m_n","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-mass-formula.lean#L49-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.MassParams.m_p","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.MassParams.m_p","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-mass-formula.lean#L48-L48","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.MassParams.m_e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.MassParams.m_e","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-mass-formula.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.MassParams.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.MassParams.q","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-mass-formula.lean#L46-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.MassParams.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.MassParams.mk","kind":"ctor","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-mass-formula.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.MassParams","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.MassParams","kind":"structure","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-mass-formula.lean#L40-L52","doc":"The mass formula parameters, all derived from `q` and `m_e`.\n\nParametrised over the ground ring `R`.  Pre-Arch: every field\nis a Laurent polynomial in `q`.  Post-Arch: every field is the\nreal evaluation at `q = q₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.ThreeInvariants.Φ₃","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.ThreeInvariants.Φ₃","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-mass-formula.lean#L38-L38","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.ThreeInvariants.Φ₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.ThreeInvariants.Φ₂","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-mass-formula.lean#L37-L37","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.ThreeInvariants.Φ₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.ThreeInvariants.Φ₁","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-mass-formula.lean#L36-L36","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.ThreeInvariants.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.ThreeInvariants.mk","kind":"ctor","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-mass-formula.lean#L35-L35","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.ThreeInvariants","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.ThreeInvariants","kind":"structure","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-mass-formula.lean#L28-L38","doc":"The three Wedderburn invariants of a transfer matrix chain.\nThese correspond to the three extremal irreps of H_n(q):\nsymmetric (dim 1), standard (dim n-1), alternating (dim 1).\n\nPolymorphic in the ground ring `R`.  The pre-Archimedean\nconvention is `R = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials); the\nArchimedean specialisation evaluates at `q ↦ q₀ ∈ ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}